{
  "id": "ep098",
  "duration": 53.438,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.02,
      "text": "Deep in the constellation Leo, there is a planet of burning ice.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Johann Elert Bode - Leo.jpg",
        "credit": "Johann Elert Bode",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Johann_Elert_Bode_-_Leo.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.733,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 2.733,
          "end": 4.033,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.02,
      "end": 12.14,
      "text": "Discovered in 2004, [Gliese](/\u0261l\u02c8iz\u02c8\u028c/) 436 b is a Neptune-sized world orbiting a red dwarf star.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Gliese-436-b.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gliese-436-b.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.033,
          "end": 8.667,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 8.667,
          "end": 12.133,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 12.14,
      "end": 17.485,
      "text": "It sits so close to its sun that it completes a full year in about 2.6 days.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "(589683) 2010 RF43 orbit diagram jpl.png",
        "credit": "Public domainPublic domainfalsefalse\n\n\n\n\n\nThis file is in the public domain in the United States because it was solely created by NASA. NASA copyright policy states that \"NASA material is not protecte",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:(589683)_2010_RF43_orbit_diagram_jpl.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 12.133,
          "end": 17.5,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 17.485,
      "end": 23.36,
      "text": "This extreme proximity bakes the planet\u2019s surface to over 800 degrees Fahrenheit.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 17.5,
          "end": 23.367,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 23.36,
      "end": 29.605,
      "text": "But the planet\u2019s gravity is so intense it crushes water into exotic ice despite that heat.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Crystal structure of ice VII.png",
        "credit": "Khsacc",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Crystal_structure_of_ice_VII.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 23.367,
          "end": 29.6,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 29.605,
      "end": 35.305,
      "text": "High-pressure physics forces the water into a dense crystal that cannot vaporize.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Water phase diagram with enlarge of supercritical region being analyzed - Widom line in red in Fig a.jpg",
        "credit": "Florentina Maxim, Cristian Contescu, Pierre Boillat, Bojan Niceno, Konstantinos Karalis, Andrea Testino, Christian Ludwig",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Water_phase_diagram_with_enlarge_of_supercritical_region_being_analyzed_-_Widom_line_in_red_in_Fig_a.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 29.6,
          "end": 32.233,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 32.233,
          "end": 35.3,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 35.305,
      "end": 41.35,
      "text": "While it holds onto its ice, the planet is actually bleeding a massive cloud of hydrogen gas.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Flickr via Openverse",
        "title": "Exoplanet with Comet-like Tail (Illustration)",
        "credit": "NASA Hubble",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://www.flickr.com/photos/144614754@N02/48790154502"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 35.3,
          "end": 38.333,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 38.333,
          "end": 41.367,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 41.35,
      "end": 48.525,
      "text": "Hubble observations show this comet-like tail stretching 50 times wider than the parent star itself.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Gliese 436 b.tiff",
        "credit": "NASA, ESA, STScI, and G. Bacon",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gliese_436_b.tiff"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 41.367,
          "end": 48.533,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 48.525,
      "end": 53.088,
      "text": "It remains a mystery of high-pressure physics, deep in the constellation Leo.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Johann Elert Bode - Leo.jpg",
        "credit": "Johann Elert Bode",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Johann_Elert_Bode_-_Leo.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 48.533,
          "end": 53.433,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
